---
id: org.dxos.plugin.github.file-sync
name: GitHub two-way file sync
version: 0.1.0
---

Two-way sync between files in a GitHub repository and ECHO objects, where the mapping from a file to
an object is contributed by another plugin. Deus specs (`*.mdl` → plugin-code's `Spec`) are the
first mapping and the case study.

This is part 2 of three (see [SYNC.mdl](SYNC.mdl)). It needs part 1's binding on `Repo`; it does
not need part 3, which only makes it react sooner.

plugin-github owns change detection, sync markers, merging and commits. The mapping plugin owns the
file format, and nothing else: it never imports plugin-github and never calls GitHub.

## Extensions

The following extension dialects are used in this document.
Each extension is defined in the Appendix or resolved via its URI.

| Term        | URI                            |
|-------------|--------------------------------|
| `type`      | `org.dxos.mdl.type@1.0`        |
| `service`   | `org.dxos.mdl.service@1.0`     |
| `op`        | `org.dxos.mdl.op@1.1`          |
| `feat`      | `org.dxos.mdl.feat@1.0`        |
| `scenario`  | `org.dxos.mdl.scenario@1.0`    |
| `decision`  | `org.dxos.mdl.decision@1.0`    |

## Diagram

A plugin-illustrator render. The `diagram` block is the source; regenerate the image with
`moon run plugin-illustrator:render-diagrams -- <abs path>/spec/diagrams/p2-sync.dx`.

![The branch head differs from the marker's commit; compare lists changed paths; matching mappings invoke plugin-code's ImportSpec, which applies the change at the marker's heads; local edits since those heads go through ExportSpec to a commit on the write branch, whose parents are its tip and the read head.](diagrams/p2-sync.dx.svg)

```diagram
diagram flow=right
group api "api.github.com" {
  node Head "branch head sha"
  node Compare "compare old...new"
  node Commit "commit on branch"
}
group github "plugin-github" {
  node Filter "match mappings" ref="packages/plugins/plugin-github/src/types/GitHubCapabilities.ts"
  node Marker "FileMarker" ref="packages/core/compute/link/src/Cursor.ts"
  node Diff "diff since heads"
}
group code "plugin-code" {
  node Import "ImportSpecFile op" ref="packages/plugins/plugin-code/src/operations/index.ts"
  node Export "ExportSpecFile op" ref="packages/plugins/plugin-code/src/operations/index.ts"
  node Spec "Spec (Text)" ref="packages/plugins/plugin-code/src/types/Spec.ts"
}
edge Head -> Compare "≠ marker commit"
edge Compare -> Filter "changed paths"
edge Filter -> Import "invoke"
edge Import -> Spec "changeAt(heads)"
edge Import -> Marker "blob, commit, heads"
edge Marker -> Diff "base heads"
edge Spec -> Diff
edge Diff -> Export "local edits"
edge Export -> Commit "write tip + read head"
```

## Extension point

### `GitHubCapabilities.FileMapping`

A plugin contributes one entry per file kind. The entry names two operations; plugin-github invokes
them, so they run wherever the sync runs (EDGE) and are tested without GitHub.

```ts
// packages/plugins/plugin-github/src/types/GitHubCapabilities.ts
import * as Schema from 'effect/Schema';

import * as Capability from '@dxos/app-framework/Capability';
import type * as Operation from '@dxos/compute/Operation';
import { Obj, Ref, type Type } from '@dxos/echo';
import { Repo } from '@dxos/types';

import { meta } from '#meta';

/** How one kind of repository file becomes an ECHO object and back. */
export type FileMapping = {
  /** Stable id, recorded on every marker the mapping writes, e.g. `org.dxos.plugin.code.spec`. */
  readonly id: string;
  /** Repository-relative globs the mapping claims, e.g. `['**\/*.mdl']`: `**` spans directories, `*` and `?` stay within one. */
  readonly match: readonly string[];
  /** The ECHO type a matched file becomes. */
  readonly type: Type.AnyObj;
  /** Pull: create the object, or apply a remote change to it. */
  readonly import: Operation.Definition<FileImportInput, FileImportOutput>;
  /** Push: render the object as file content. Absent → the mapping is pull-only. */
  readonly export?: Operation.Definition<FileExportInput, FileExportOutput>;
  /** Largest file the engine imports for this mapping; larger files are skipped and reported. Default 1 MiB. */
  readonly maxBytes?: number;
};

export const FileImportInput = Schema.Struct({
  repository: Ref.Ref(Repo.Repo),
  path: Schema.String,
  /** The file as the new commit has it (UTF-8). */
  content: Schema.String,
  /** The file as the marker's commit had it; absent on first import. */
  base: Schema.optional(Schema.String),
  /** The object the marker binds; absent on first import. */
  object: Schema.optional(Ref.Ref(Obj.Unknown)),
  /** The object's Automerge heads at the last sync: apply the base → content change as of these. */
  heads: Schema.optional(Schema.Array(Schema.String)),
});
export interface FileImportInput extends Schema.Schema.Type<typeof FileImportInput> {}

export const FileImportOutput = Schema.Struct({
  object: Ref.Ref(Obj.Unknown),
  /** The heads at which the object holds exactly `content`, recorded on the marker. */
  heads: Schema.Array(Schema.String),
});
export interface FileImportOutput extends Schema.Schema.Type<typeof FileImportOutput> {}

export const FileExportInput = Schema.Struct({
  object: Ref.Ref(Obj.Unknown),
  path: Schema.String,
  /** The file as GitHub holds it for this space: the blob last pushed while unmerged, else the blob last synced. */
  base: Schema.optional(Schema.String),
});
export interface FileExportInput extends Schema.Schema.Type<typeof FileExportInput> {}

export const FileExportOutput = Schema.Struct({
  content: Schema.String,
  /** The heads the content was rendered from, recorded on the marker after the commit lands. */
  heads: Schema.Array(Schema.String),
});
export interface FileExportOutput extends Schema.Schema.Type<typeof FileExportOutput> {}

// One contribution per mapping; plugin-github reads them with `Capability.getAll`.
export const FileMapping = Capability.make<FileMapping>()(`${meta.profile.key}.capability.fileMapping`);
```

```mdl
service FileMapping
  desc: Capability contributed by a plugin that owns a file format. plugin-github calls its operations; it never calls GitHub.
  ops:
    import(repository: Ref<Repo>, path: string, content: string, base?: string, object?: Ref<Obj>, heads?: string[]) → { object: Ref<Obj>, heads: string[] }
    export(object: Ref<Obj>, path: string, base?: string) → { content: string, heads: string[] }
  errors:
    MappingParseError: the file does not parse as the mapping's format; the file is skipped and reported, the object is untouched
```

### `TextMerge` helper

Most mappings hold the file body as `Text`. plugin-github exports the merge they share, so a mapping's
`import` is a few lines.

```ts
// packages/plugins/plugin-github/src/file-sync/TextMerge.ts (exported as @dxos/plugin-github/TextMerge)
/**
 * Apply the `base` → `next` change to `text` as of `heads`, so Automerge merges it with every local
 * edit made since. Returns the heads at which `text` holds exactly `next` (the change's own heads).
 */
export const applyAt: (
  text: Text.Text,
  change: { readonly base: string; readonly next: string; readonly heads: readonly string[] },
) => Effect.Effect<readonly string[], TextMergeError>;

/** True when `text` differs from its content at `heads`: the object has local edits to push. */
export const changedSince: (text: Text.Text, heads: readonly string[]) => Effect.Effect<boolean>;
```

```mdl
service TextMerge
  desc: Helpers shared by Text-backed mappings.
  ops:
    applyAt(text: Text, base: string, next: string, heads: string[]) → string[]
    changedSince(text: Text, heads: string[]) → boolean
  errors:
    TextMergeError: the heads are not in the object's history (the object was replaced)
```

## Types

### File binding

File sync is its own `Cursor`, separate from part 1's item cursor, bound to the same `Repo`. Its
`token` is a commit SHA, not an ETag, which is why it cannot share part 1's cursor.

```ts
// How the file binding reads Cursor (packages/core/compute/link/src/Cursor.ts).
type FileBinding = Cursor.ExternalCursor & {
  spec: {
    kind: 'external';
    source: Ref.Ref<AccessToken.AccessToken>;
    target: Ref.Ref<Repo.Repo>;
    externalId: string;                     // GitHub numeric repository id
    /** The last commit fully synced on `options.branch`. */
    token?: string;
    options: FileSyncOptions;
    /** `file:<path>` → FileMarker; `history:<path>` → VersionLink[]. */
    snapshots?: Record<string, FileMarker | readonly VersionLink[]>;
  };
};
```

```mdl
type FileSyncOptions
  desc: Per-binding options for file sync.
  fields:
    stream: files                 # tells the sync handler this cursor is a file binding
    branch: string                # branch read from, e.g. main
    writeBranch: string           # branch written to; default composer/<spaceId>; never equal to branch
    mappings?: string[]           # FileMapping ids to run; omit for every contributed mapping
    paths?: string[]              # extra globs that narrow every mapping, e.g. packages/plugins/**
```

```mdl
type FileMarker
  desc: Sync state for one file. Stored at Cursor.spec.snapshots["file:<path>"].
  fields:
    mapping: string               # FileMapping.id that owns the file
    path: string
    blob: string                  # git blob SHA last synced
    commit: string                # commit the blob was read from or written to
    heads: string[]               # the object's heads at which it holds exactly the blob
    object: Ref<Obj>
    pushed?: { blob: string, heads: string[], commit: string }   # what this space last committed for the file, until the read branch carries it
```

The binding's write state sits beside the markers at `snapshots.state`: the read branch's ETag, the
newest commit this space wrote (`lastWritten`), the read head that commit merged in, and the pull
request.

```mdl
type VersionLink
  desc: One synced version: a commit and the object heads that hold the same content. Capped at 50 per file, oldest dropped.
  fields:
    commit: string
    heads: string[]
    at: string                    # ISO time the sync recorded it
    direction: pull | push
```

The object itself carries a foreign key, so a file renamed on either side is re-keyed rather than
duplicated:

```ts
// Meta key on every object a mapping imports.
{ source: 'github.com', id: `${repoId}:${path}` }
```

### GitHub payloads

```mdl
type CompareFile
  desc: One entry of GET /repos/{o}/{r}/compare/{base}...{head} → files[].
  fields:
    filename: string
    previous_filename?: string    # set when status is renamed
    status: added | modified | removed | renamed | copied | changed
    sha: string                   # new blob SHA
```

## Services

`GitHubApi` gains git reads and writes.

```ts
// Added to packages/plugins/plugin-github/src/services/github-api.ts.
/** GET /repos/{o}/{r}/git/ref/heads/{branch} with If-None-Match. */
export const fetchBranchHead: (owner: string, repo: string, branch: string, etag?: string) =>
  GitHubEffect<Conditional<{ sha: string }>>;

/** GET /repos/{o}/{r}/compare/{base}...{head}; `truncated` when GitHub listed more than 300 files. */
export const compareCommits: (owner: string, repo: string, base: string, head: string) =>
  GitHubEffect<{ files: readonly CompareFile[]; truncated: boolean }>;

/** GET /repos/{o}/{r}/git/trees/{sha}?recursive=1, the fallback when compare is truncated. */
export const fetchTree: (owner: string, repo: string, sha: string) =>
  GitHubEffect<readonly { path: string; sha: string; type: 'blob' | 'tree'; size?: number }[]>;

/** GET /repos/{o}/{r}/git/blobs/{sha}, decoded to UTF-8. */
export const fetchBlob: (owner: string, repo: string, sha: string) => GitHubEffect<string>;

/** Blob → tree (on `baseTree`) → commit (on `parents`, in order) → ref update, never forced. */
export const commitFiles: (
  owner: string,
  repo: string,
  input: {
    branch: string;
    parents: readonly string[];   // the write branch's tip, then the read head when it is merged in
    baseTree: string;
    message: string;
    files: readonly { path: string; content: string | null }[];   // null deletes
  },
) => GitHubEffect<{ commit: string; blobs: Record<string, string> }, RefMovedError>;

/** Open the write branch's pull request, or return the open one. */
export const ensurePullRequest: (
  owner: string,
  repo: string,
  input: { head: string; base: string; title: string; body: string },
) => GitHubEffect<{ number: number; url: string }>;
```

```mdl
service GitHubApi
  desc: Git reads and writes added for file sync.
  ops:
    fetchBranchHead(owner: string, repo: string, branch: string, etag?: string) → Conditional<{ sha: string }>
    compareCommits(owner: string, repo: string, base: string, head: string) → { files: CompareFile[], truncated: boolean }
    fetchTree(owner: string, repo: string, sha: string) → TreeEntry[]
    fetchBlob(owner: string, repo: string, sha: string) → string
    commitFiles(owner: string, repo: string, branch: string, parents: string[], baseTree: string, message: string, files: FileChange[]) → { commit: string, blobs: Record<string, string> }
    ensurePullRequest(owner: string, repo: string, head: string, base: string, title: string, body: string) → { number: number, url: string }
  errors:
    RefMovedError: the branch moved after it was read; pull again and retry
```

## Operations

```mdl
op EnableGitHubFileSync
  key: org.dxos.operation.github.enableFileSync
  desc: |
    Adds a file binding next to a repository's item binding, with the same credential and repository
    id. Returns the existing file binding when there is one. Visible, and a tool of the GitHub skill, so
    the Composer agent and the MCP server can call it.
  input:
    repository: Ref<Repo>
    branch?: string               # default: the repository's default branch
    writeBranch?: string
    mappings?: string[]
    paths?: string[]
  output: { binding: string, created: boolean }
  effects: [echo:read, echo:write]
```

One pass over a file binding runs inside `SyncGitHubRepositories`, which hands every cursor whose
`options.stream` is `files` to the file-sync engine (`syncFileBinding`) and every other cursor to part
1's poll. Its output gains `files: { pulled, pushed, skipped }`. A pass fails with
`GitHubRefMovedError` when the write branch moved three times in a row; the next pass retries.

```mdl
type FileSyncResult
  fields:
    requests: number
    pulled: number
    pushed: number
    skipped: { path: string, reason: string }[]
    pullRequest?: { number: number, url: string }
```

plugin-code contributes the Deus mapping:

```mdl
op ImportSpecFile
  key: org.dxos.operation.code.importSpecFile
  desc: FileMapping.import for `**/*.mdl`. Creates a Spec, or applies the change to Spec.content with TextMerge.applyAt.
  input: FileImportInput
  output: FileImportOutput
  effects: [echo:read, echo:write]
```

```mdl
op ExportSpecFile
  key: org.dxos.operation.code.exportSpecFile
  desc: FileMapping.export for `**/*.mdl`. Returns Spec.content as it stands, with the heads it read; a document a codec writes is rendered against base.
  input: FileExportInput
  output: FileExportOutput
  effects: [echo:read]
```

## Features

```mdl
feat F-1: Mapping contract

  req F-1.1: A plugin adds a file kind by contributing a GitHubCapabilities.FileMapping entry; plugin-github has no code for any file format.

  req F-1.2: When two mappings match one path, the one contributed first wins and the conflict is logged once per pass.

  req F-1.3: A mapping without `export` is pull-only; local edits to its objects are never pushed and are overwritten only where the remote changed the same text.
```

```mdl
feat F-2: Change detection

  req F-2.1:
    when: a file binding is synced
    then: the first request is fetchBranchHead with the stored ETag

  req F-2.2:
    when: the branch head equals Cursor.spec.token, no bound object changed since its marker's heads, and the write branch (when it exists) is still at the commit this space last wrote
    then: the pass ends; that is one request, or two while a write branch exists

  req F-2.3:
    when: the head moved
    then: compareCommits(token, head) lists the changed paths in one request; when it reports truncated, two fetchTree calls are diffed instead, and a removed path and an added path with the same blob SHA count as a rename

  req F-2.4: Only blobs for paths a mapping matches, and that are at most maxBytes, are fetched.
```

```mdl
feat F-3: Pull

  req F-3.1:
    when: a matched path is added
    then: import runs without base, object or heads, and a FileMarker is written

  req F-3.2:
    when: a matched path is modified
    then: import runs with base = the blob at marker.blob, the marker's object and heads; the change lands as of those heads and Automerge merges it with local edits made since

  req F-3.3:
    when: a path is renamed
    then: the object's foreign key and the marker move to the new path; no object is created

  req F-3.4:
    when: a path is removed
    then: the marker is dropped and the object is kept, without its foreign key; deleting a remote file never deletes local content
```

```mdl
feat F-4: Push

  req F-4.1:
    when: a bound object's content differs from its content at marker.heads
    then: export renders it, after this pass's pulls, so the pushed content contains both sides

  req F-4.2: Every changed file in a pass goes into one commit on options.writeBranch. Its first parent is the write branch's tip; when the head just pulled from options.branch is not in the write branch's history, that head is the second parent, so the commit both fast-forwards the write branch and merges the read branch into it. A missing write branch is created at the pulled head. The commit's tree is the read head's tree with the current export of every bound object whose content differs from its blob there, so it carries both the read branch's changes and every Composer edit not yet merged; the two cannot conflict, because the pull has already merged them in each object. The ref update is never forced.

  req F-4.3:
    when: the ref update fails with RefMovedError
    then: the pass reads the write branch's tip again, re-exports and retries, at most three times

  req F-4.4: The write branch has one open pull request into options.branch; the pass opens it or reuses it. Nothing is written to options.branch.

  req F-4.5: Pushed edits are attributed to the connection's GitHub account; the commit message names the space and the Composer users whose edits it carries.

  req F-4.6:
    when: the write branch's tip is not a commit this space wrote (the newest push VersionLink)
    then: the paths changed since that commit are pulled before anything is exported: a modified path as in F-3.2 with base = the blob this space last pushed, an added path as in F-3.1, a renamed path as in F-3.3 (with any content change applied as in F-3.2), and a removed path as in F-3.4. A removed path, and a renamed path's old name, are also removed from the push tree, so F-4.2 does not restore them from the read head; a person's commit on the pull request is merged, never overwritten. The space's own commits are never pulled, since they carry edits it already holds

  req F-4.7: Export is given base, the file as GitHub holds it for this space: the blob in marker.pushed while that is set, else marker.blob. The engine reads it from a cache of blob contents by SHA that every blob a pass fetches or pushes fills, so it costs a fetchBlob only when the process has not read or written that blob.
```

```mdl
feat F-5: Markers and version tracking

  req F-5.1: Cursor.spec.token and every FileMarker the pass wrote advance in one Obj.update, so a crash leaves either the old state or the new one.

  req F-5.2: Each pull and push appends a VersionLink pairing the commit with the object's heads; the newest 50 are kept per file.

  req F-5.3: Given a commit, the object version is the heads of its VersionLink; given heads, the commit is the newest VersionLink whose heads they contain.
```

```mdl
feat F-6: Deus specs

  req F-6.1: plugin-code contributes the mapping `org.dxos.plugin.code.spec` for `**/*.mdl`, typed `Spec`, with ImportSpecFile and ExportSpecFile.

  req F-6.2: Spec.content is Text, so specs merge character by character. A spec a `ProjectCapabilities.SpecCodec` writes merges as the file text the codec renders, which the codec reads back; the engine runs no `.mdl` parser itself.
```

## Acceptance

```mdl
scenario T-1: Nothing changed
  given: a file binding whose token equals the branch head; no Spec changed locally; no write branch exists
  when: SyncGitHubFiles runs
  then:
    - one request is made and GitHub answers 304
    - no object, marker or token changes
```

```mdl
scenario T-2: Remote edit
  given: a synced PLUGIN.mdl; a commit on main changes one requirement line
  when: SyncGitHubFiles runs
  then:
    - requests are fetchBranchHead, compareCommits and two fetchBlob calls (new and base)
    - Spec.content shows the new line; FileMarker.blob, commit and heads advance
```

```mdl
scenario T-3: Concurrent edits
  given: a synced PLUGIN.mdl; a Composer user edits F-1 while a commit on main edits F-3
  when: SyncGitHubFiles runs
  then:
    - Spec.content holds both edits
    - one commit on composer/<spaceId> carries the F-1 edit, with parents = the write branch's tip and the new main head
    - the write branch's pull request is opened or updated
```

```mdl
scenario T-4: Write branch moved
  given: local edits to push; another client pushes to the write branch between read and write
  when: SyncGitHubFiles runs
  then:
    - the first ref update fails with RefMovedError
    - the pass reads the write branch's tip again, re-exports, and the second update succeeds
```

```mdl
scenario T-5: File removed upstream
  given: a synced spec whose file is deleted on main
  when: SyncGitHubFiles runs
  then:
    - the marker is gone and the Spec still exists without its github.com key
```

## Open questions

Both questions this section held are settled; see D-14.

## Changelog

```mdl
decision D-1: Part 2 of the GitHub sync design is extensible two-way sync. Another plugin defines how to sync its files (specs) into ECHO, and plugin-github schedules it by calling that plugin's operation. It has an ontology for sync markers, uses Automerge heads and GitHub commits for version tracking, and merges and rebases changes with Automerge `changeAt`. It is extensible, takes Deus specs as the case study, and must be efficient.
  date: 2026-10-21
  by: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [F-1, F-2, F-3, F-4, F-5, F-6]
  source: https://claude.ai/code/session_01BvVEssur2xxCiXewKjKQ3Z
```

```mdl
decision D-2: A mapping is a FileMapping capability entry naming an import and an optional export operation; TextMerge is the shared helper for Text-backed mappings. Fills in [D-1].
  date: 2026-10-21
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [FileMapping, TextMerge, F-1]
  why: Operations run on EDGE wherever the sync runs and are testable without GitHub, and the mapping plugin needs no dependency on plugin-github beyond the capability type.
  rejected:
    - A plain function on the capability: cannot be invoked on EDGE through the operation registry.
```

```mdl
decision D-3: Markers live on a separate file Cursor (token = commit SHA) as snapshots `file:<path>`, with up to 50 VersionLinks per file. Fills in [D-1].
  date: 2026-10-21
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [FileMarker, VersionLink, FileSyncOptions, F-5]
  why: Part 1's cursor uses token for an ETag; one token per cursor keeps Cursor.writeSyncState's paired update.
  rejected:
    - A SyncMarker relation object per file: one more ECHO object per file for state only the sync reads.
```

```mdl
decision D-4: Detection is one branch-head request, then one compare; pushes go to a write branch with a pull request, never to the read branch, with a non-forced ref update retried at most three times. Fills in [D-1].
  date: 2026-10-21
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [F-2, F-4]
  why: A quiet repository costs one request that GitHub answers 304; a branch and pull request keep a review step between Composer edits and main.
```

```mdl
decision D-5: A file deleted upstream keeps its local object and drops only the marker and foreign key. Fills in [D-1].
  date: 2026-10-21
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [F-3.4]
  why: A sync must never delete content a user may still be editing; removing it stays a user action.
```

```mdl
decision D-6: A push commit's first parent is the write branch's tip, and the read branch's pulled head is a second parent when the write branch does not already contain it. The write branch's own commits are never pulled. Narrows [D-4], whose parent was the pulled head.
  date: 2026-10-22
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [F-4.2, F-4.3, T-3, T-4]
  why: The write branch lives across passes, so a commit parented only on the read branch's head stops descending from it once the read branch moves, and a non-forced update would be rejected on every retry.
  rejected:
    - Force-resetting the write branch to each new commit: drops commits a reviewer may have pushed onto the pull request.
```

```mdl
decision D-7: When compareCommits is truncated and two trees are diffed instead, a removed and an added path with the same blob SHA are paired as a rename; anything unpaired is a removal plus an addition.
  date: 2026-10-22
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [F-2.3, F-3.3]
  why: A tree diff carries no rename information, and without pairing F-3.3 would duplicate a renamed file as a new object.
```

```mdl
decision D-8: A push commit's tree is the read head's tree plus the export of every bound object that differs from it; `commitFiles` takes ordered parents. Commits on the write branch that this space did not write are pulled before export. Fills in [D-6].
  date: 2026-10-22
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [commitFiles, F-4.2, F-4.6]
  why: Two parents alone do not combine trees, and a tree built from either side alone dropped the other's changes; exporting from ECHO, where the pull has already merged both sides, gives one tree with no conflicts. A reviewer's commit on the pull request is the one write-branch change ECHO does not already hold, so it is pulled rather than overwritten.
```

```mdl
decision D-9: The quiet-pass check also reads the write branch's head, and F-4.6 routes a person's added, modified and removed paths through F-3.1, F-3.2 and F-3.4. Fills in [D-8].
  date: 2026-10-22
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [F-2.2, F-4.6]
  why: Without the second read a reviewer's commit waited for some unrelated change to be noticed, and treating every path as a modification left added files without an object and let removed files come back from the read head's tree.
```

```mdl
decision D-10: F-4.6 also routes a person's renamed path through F-3.3, applying any content change in the same step. Fills in [D-9].
  date: 2026-10-22
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [F-4.6]
  why: compareCommits reports a rename as its own status, and without a rule for it the pass would neither re-key the object nor keep the old path from returning.
```

```mdl
decision D-11: A person's rename on the write branch removes the old name from the push tree, as a removal does. Fills in [D-10].
  date: 2026-10-22
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [F-4.6]
  why: F-4.2 starts the push tree from the read head, which still holds the old name until the pull request merges, so the next push would otherwise bring the file back beside its new name.
```

```mdl
decision D-12: plugin-code's operations are ImportSpecFile and ExportSpecFile, and FileMapping is one capability contribution per mapping, read with `Capability.getAll`. Narrows [D-2].
  date: 2026-10-27
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [FileMapping, ImportSpecFile, ExportSpecFile, F-1, F-6.1]
  why: `org.dxos.operation.code.importSpec` already names plugin-code's import from a local checkout, and every other multi-plugin capability contributes one entry per plugin. `Type.Obj.Any` does not exist; `Type.AnyObj` is the same type. Globs use a small matcher in plugin-github (`**`, `*`, `?`), because no shipped package depends on picomatch.
```

```mdl
decision D-13: There is no SyncGitHubFiles operation; SyncGitHubRepositories runs a file binding's pass in process, and EnableGitHubFileSync creates the binding. Narrows [D-4].
  date: 2026-10-27
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [EnableGitHubFileSync, FileSyncResult, F-2]
  why: The sync Routine already invokes SyncGitHubRepositories with the connection, and `Binding.syncAll` fans out over every cursor of it; a second operation would need its own invocation per binding for no gain. Without an operation that adds the cursor, nothing could turn file sync on.
```

```mdl
decision D-14: A marker keeps what this space pushed (`pushed`) until the read branch carries it. A pull whose blob equals it adopts it without an import; once the write branch's commit is in the read head, a pull's base is the pushed content at the pushed heads. Local changes are found by exporting each object and comparing its git blob SHA with `pushed ?? blob`. This settles both open questions: `changeAt` is reachable through `Doc.createAccessor(...).handle`, and `Binding.syncAll` runs both cursors of one Repo. Fills in [D-8].
  date: 2026-10-27
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [FileMarker, TextMerge, F-2.2, F-3.2, F-4.1]
  why: After a merge, the read branch holds this space's own edits; applying old-base → new at the old heads would insert them a second time. Comparing SHAs works for any mapping and costs no request. Telling whether the write branch was merged costs one compare per pass, only while a write is outstanding and the read head moved.
```

```mdl
decision D-15: F-4.5's per-user attribution and F-4.6's pull from the write branch are not built yet. A pass whose write-branch tip is not the commit it last wrote holds its push back and reports each file as skipped; a commit names the space only. F-4.3's retry re-parents on the re-read tip. F-5.3's lookups are left to the first caller; the VersionLinks they read are recorded. Defers part of [D-9].
  date: 2026-10-27
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [F-4.3, F-4.5, F-4.6, F-5.3, T-4]
  why: Holding the push back cannot overwrite a reviewer's commit, which is what F-4.6 protects, and keeps the first version small; the skipped entries show the user why nothing was pushed. compareCommits does not report sizes, so F-2.4's limit is checked after the fetch when the change came from a compare.
```

```mdl
decision D-16: EnableGitHubFileSync is a visible operation and a tool of the GitHub skill, whose instructions tell the agent to call it with the repository's Repo object. Fills in [D-13].
  date: 2026-10-29
  by: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [EnableGitHubFileSync]
  why: With no button and no tool, nothing could turn file sync on; the Composer agent and the MCP server reach operations only through visible operations and skills.
```

```mdl
decision D-17: A spec file synced from a GitHub repository is read into features embedded in its document, as a file synced from a local checkout is. Refines [D-12].
  date: 2026-10-29
  by: user:wittjosiah
  affects: [F-6.2]
```

```mdl
decision D-18: The engine passes export the file text it renders against, fetched once per file and cached by blob SHA, so a push does not wait for a pull on the same device. Refines [D-17].
  date: 2026-10-29
  by: user:wittjosiah
  affects: [F-4.7, FileExportInput]
```

```mdl
decision D-19: The base is the blob in marker.pushed while that is set, else marker.blob. The cache lives for the process, is bounded at 16 MiB and evicts the least recently used blob; the pull's own fetchBlob calls are unchanged, so T-2's requests stand. Fills in [D-18].
  date: 2026-10-29
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:wittjosiah
  affects: [F-4.7, T-1]
  why: The pushed blob is what the write branch holds, so an export against it keeps the form of what was pushed. A blob SHA names its content, so a cached entry never goes stale; the first pass of a process pays one fetchBlob per bound file it has not read, and every later quiet pass costs T-1's one request.
  rejected:
    - Fetching the base on every pass, which costs one request per bound file and breaks T-1.
    - Keeping the base per device, where a push on a device that has not pulled the file waits for the next pull.
```

```mdl
decision D-20: The FileMapping service's `export` takes `base`, as FileExportInput does. Fills in [D-18].
  date: 2026-10-30
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:wittjosiah
  affects: [FileMapping]
  why: D-18 added `base` to FileExportInput and F-4.7 has the engine pass it, but the service block still declared export without it.
```

```mdl
decision D-21: A spec's text is its own `content`; there is no separate spec document.
  date: 2026-10-30
  by: user:wittjosiah
  affects: [F-6.2]
```

```mdl
decision D-22: The codec is renamed `ProjectCapabilities.SpecCodec` and writes a spec. A spec no codec takes merges as plain text. Fills in [D-21].
  date: 2026-10-30
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:wittjosiah
  affects: [F-6.2]
  why: The codec's subject is now the spec itself, and a prose spec keeps the character merge F-6.2 gives every spec.
```
